 "notes": [
  "The byline 'Darth Vader \"The Dark\" Lord of The Sith' is a prank name; the deck is credited to the DeckTech handle The Dark as plain text (no player page), as with deck 18394 (this deck's v 2).",
  "Starting cards as posted under 'Starting (5)': Quiet Mining Colony / Independent Operation, Bespin, Cloud City: West Gallery, The Signal and Beldon's Eye; these count toward the 60. The Signal is not a starting interrupt by its text, so no starting interrupt is set.",
  "The deck totals 58 as published. The section headers do not all match the lists (Characters 21 vs 22 listed, Starships 13 vs 14).",
  "Format Premiere - Tatooine: no Coruscant-set card in the list.",
  "Posted 'Cloud City Docking Bay 327' dested Cloud City: Platform 327 (Docking Bay); 'Cloud City Guest Chambers' dested Cloud City: Guest Quarters; 'Cloud City Upper Plaza Corridor' dested the Light Cloud City: Upper Plaza Corridor.",
  "Posted 'Moving Into Attack Position' dested Moving To Attack Position; 'Mirax' dested Mirax Terrik; 'R2-D2 in Red 5' dested Artoo-Detoo In Red 5; 'Cloud City Technichian' and 'Red Sqaudron 7' are spelling slips.",
  "The strategy's update says the Seekers (Tagge, Tarkin, Motti Seeker) were later swapped for Obi-Wan, his Lightsaber and another Tibanna Gas Miner; the list is kept as published."
 ],
